@startuml fig-2-7-activity-training
' Figure 2.7 — Activity diagram, offline model training pipeline
!theme plain
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12

start
:Acquire raw corpora
(PhishTank verified feed, path-bearing benign corpus);
:Retain submission_time, target, verified, online;
:Filter to verified == yes;
:Deduplicate on registrable domain;
:Write data/processed/dataset.csv;

:Run leakage audit;
note right
  Reports single-feature ROC-AUC,
  class-conditional means and
  path-presence rate per class.
end note

if (Any single feature exceeds 0.90 AUC alone?) then (yes)
  :Investigate the artefact;
  :Re-source or rebalance the affected class;
  detach
else (no)
endif

:Extract features for every row;
:Drop the three VirusTotal columns (ADR-013);
:Write data/processed/features.csv;

:Split temporally on submission_time;
:Enforce disjoint registrable domains
across train and test;

:Train XGBoost classifier;
:Write model.pkl and feature_columns.json
in a single atomic step;

if (model.n_features_in_ == len(feature_columns)?) then (no)
  :Abort with both values reported;
  stop
else (yes)
endif

:Evaluate against baselines;
:Measure calibration and explanation faithfulness;
:Write ml/reports/evaluation_report.md;
stop

note right
  Two further, separate tools consume
  this pipeline's output rather than
  extending its linear flow:
  cross_validate.py repeats the split
  and training steps under multiple
  seeds for confidence intervals
  (§5.9.1); retrain_gate.py re-runs
  the leakage audit and a candidate
  training run, promoting only if it
  does not regress against the
  incumbent model (§4.7's algorithm
  notes).
end note
@enduml
